<h1>Interactive Noise Reduction by Curvature</h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mesh &gt; Reduce Noise &gt; Interactive</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Interactive Noise Reduction By Curvature</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command modifies the visible selection based on the local surrounding data and local curvature. Every point has a normal defined by the normals of the surrounding triangles. The curvature is described by the maximum angle between that normal and normals of the neighbour points (see</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="Point_Curvature.htm">Point Curvature</a></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">for details.) The flatter the area is the stronger the filter is. The smaller the curvature is, the flatter the surface is. The noise reduction is small if the curvature is high in order to keep the mesh features unchanged. So the noise will be mostly eliminated on a flat surface.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected entities as well as on partial selections.</span></p>
<p>Select a noisy area and call <span class="Command">Interactive Noise Reduction By Curvature</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command. The following dialog will appear:</span></p>
<p class="whs4"><img src="../Mesh/images/interactive_noise_reduction_by_curvature.jpg" width="228px" height="239px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Max</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Specifies the maximum offset of the points from their original counterparts. Maximum offset is calculated on the basis of the strength and maximum curvature. You can only reduce that parameter. Default value is 1000 mm.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Preview button</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Updates the colour error plot of the magnitude of changes that will be made to the selection according to the values of Max, Strength, and Maximum curvature.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Strength</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Specifies how strong a filter to apply, i.e. number of iterations. Default value is Strength = 1.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Maximum curvature to apply noise reduction</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">If the local curvature is greater than the given value, the filter is not applied in this area. It ranges from 1 to 40. Default value is maximum curvature = 7 degrees.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">When you are ready with the settings, press</span> <span class="Button">OK</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to apply the filter. This command uses the same algorithm as</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Command" style="text-decoration:none;">Noise Reduction By Curvature</span></u><span lang="EN-GB">. The advantages are that you can limit the maximum offset of the points and preview the magnitude of changes.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">After the filter has been applied and if the error map checkbox is enabled a colour error plot displays the magnitude of changes made to the selection:</span></p>
<p><img src="../Mesh/Processing_Polylines_files/Image14.gif" width="457px" height="280px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP232776745" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
