<p><span lang="EN-GB">Using</span> <span class="Command">Select By Curvature</span> <span lang="EN-GB">and</span> <span class="Command">Invert Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">you can select the flatter areas and apply any noise reduction filter (like</span> <span class="Command">Average Noise Reduction</span><span lang="EN-GB">.) But</span> <span class="Command">Interactive Noise Reduction By Curvature</span> <span lang="EN-GB">can perform such task at once.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Interactive Noise Reduction By Curvature</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to preview and then eliminate the noise on the flatter areas and to preserve features.</span></p>
